From: mx-kernel
Subject: [PATCH] Declare a cmake_minimum_required policy range

CMake 3.31+ warns that compatibility with cmake_minimum_required below 3.10
is deprecated and will be removed:

    CMake Warning (deprecated) at CMakeLists.txt:10 (cmake_minimum_required):
      Compatibility with CMake < 3.10 will be removed from a future version
      of CMake.

      Update the VERSION argument <min> value.  Or, use the <min>...<max>
      syntax to tell CMake that the project requires at least <min> but has
      been updated to work with policies introduced by <max> or earlier.

Under CMake 4.x this is not merely noise: the bare <min> form is on a path to
being removed outright, at which point the vendored tree stops configuring.

Take the second option the warning offers. The <min>...<max> range keeps the
declared floor at 3.8 -- so the project still builds with older CMake -- while
telling CMake the sources have been checked against policies up to 3.31. The
bundled nlohmann/json already uses this form (VERSION 3.5...4.0), which is why
it never produced the warning.

Verified with CMake 4.4.2: unit tests pass and the external builds, links and
signs unchanged.

Applies to: xeus 5.2.4
Upstream: not yet reported -- see patches/README.md

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 # The full license is in the file LICENSE, distributed with this software. #
 ############################################################################
 
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.8)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.8...3.31)
 project(xeus)
 
 set(CMAKE_MODULE_PATH "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/cmake;${CMAKE_MODULE_PATH}")
